61-# remedy_for prints the first line of advice for a message, keyed on a substring
62-# of it. It is a lookup rather than a per-check argument so that adding a check
63-# means adding a remedy rather than remembering to thread one through, and so
64-# the text lives in exactly one place and cannot drift from what it explains.
65-#
66-# When nothing matches, nothing is printed: a wrong remedy would send an agent
67-# chasing a problem it does not have, which is worse than the bare verdict it
